desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Insecure Random"
	title_zh: "Insecure Random"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-insecure-random"
	risk: "weak-randomness"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from rule `insecure-random` (scala/lang/security/audit/insecure-random.yaml).
Original message: Flags the use of a predictable random value from `scala.util.Random`. This can lead to vulnerabilities when used in security contexts, such as in a CSRF token, password reset token, or any other secret value. To fix this, use java.security.SecureRandom instead.
CWE: CWE-330: Use of Insufficiently Random Values
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.scala": <<<POS
import scala.util.Random
POS
	"safefile://pos.scala": <<<NEG
import scala.collection.mutable.ArrayBuffer
NEG
)

${*.scala}.pattern_regex(/(?:import\s+scala\.util\.Random)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Insecure Random",
	title_zh: "Insecure Random",
	message: "Insecure Random detected.",
}
